libretro-core.c: MMU model option

A 68030, 68040 or 68060 always gets a full MMU here: the cpu_model option writes
mmu_model=<cpu> for any of them, and the A4030/A4040 presets do the same. There was no way to
run one without MMU emulation (faster, and what an A4000/030's 68EC030 really is) or as an EC
CPU, and a config row cannot change it, because cpu_model rewrites changed_prefs.mmu_model on
every option update while running.

- puae_mmu_model: auto (the core's choice), full, ec or none.
- adm_machine_overrides_config() appends mmu_model= after the preset's row, against the CPU
  the cpu_model option resolves to; adm_machine_overrides_runtime() re-applies it, and
  mmu_ec, after every option update.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

